<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch-review-and-suggestions" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Editorial Review: Suggestions and Inconsistencies</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      This chapter is an editorial appendix rather than instructional material. It
      tracks review findings for the manual: the items already addressed in this
      revision, and those still outstanding. It is intended as a working checklist for
      the author and can be removed from the final published version once the remaining
      items have been resolved.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <!-- ============================================================= -->
  <section xml:id="sec-review-resolved">
    <title>Resolved in This Revision</title>

    <p>The following corrections have been applied to the source:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>
          <term>Cross-references.</term> Hard-coded chapter and section numbers
          (<q>See Chapter 5</q>, <q>Section 1.2</q>, etc.) have been replaced with
          PreTeXt <c>&lt;xref&gt;</c> elements that resolve automatically. This fixed
          the two factually incorrect references — the <q>Chapter 3 Scales and
          Intervals</q> pointer in the Chords chapter, and the <q>Section 13.5</q>
          pointer to the <q>How High the Moon</q> score.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          <term>Chapter identifiers.</term> The scales and modes chapters now use the
          <c>ch-</c> prefix (<c>ch-scales</c>, <c>ch-scales-modes-and-chords</c>) in
          line with every other chapter.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          <term>Filename with a space.</term> <c>sec-intervals-C natural-minor-scale.ptx</c>
          was renamed to <c>sec-intervals-C-natural-minor-scale.ptx</c> and the
          <c>xi:include</c> updated.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          <term>Roman-numeral case.</term> The diatonic-seventh-chord table now uses
          lowercase for minor degrees (ii, iii, vi) and <c>vii°</c> for the
          half-diminished degree, matching the Chord Progressions chapter.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          <term>Chord symbols.</term> The Grip Method chapter now writes
          <c>maj7♭5</c> with a proper flat sign instead of a plain <c>b</c>.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          <term>Spelling.</term> Corrected <q>seperated</q>, <q>circe</q>,
          <q>independantly</q>, <q>dependant</q>, and the possessive <q>its'</q>.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          <term>Dead markup.</term> Removed the <q>content tbe</q> placeholder from the
          first interval grid, and moved the stray caption text in the Circle of Fifths
          figure out of the rendered body.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          <term>Metadata.</term> The copyright year range now ends in 2026, and the
          frontmatter website link's target now matches its displayed text.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          <term>Index.</term> The backmatter <c>&lt;index&gt;</c> has been enabled and
          seeded with <c>&lt;idx&gt;</c> entries on the principal defined terms
          (interval, chord, triad, diatonic chord, seventh chord, chord progression,
          circle of fifths, mode, chord voicing, the Grip Method, and the Barry Harris
          system). Further entries can be added as the text grows.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================================================= -->
  <section xml:id="sec-review-outstanding">
    <title>Outstanding Items</title>

    <p>The following are left for the author's decision:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>
          <term>Attribution and permissions.</term> The additional-information chapter
          credits Jens Larsen's videos, and the Barry Harris chapter builds directly on
          Harris's teaching. Confirm that reproducing these exercises and any quoted
          material is compatible with the CC BY-SA 4.0 licence stated in the
          frontmatter, and add explicit source citations. <em>(Deferred for now.)</em>
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          <term>Commented-out includes.</term> The opening chapter still carries
          commented <c>xi:include</c> lines for <c>sec-treble-keyboard-layout</c>,
          <c>sec-free-bass-keyboard-layout</c> and <c>sec-stradella-bass-keyboard-layout</c>.
          Decide whether those sections are superseded (delete the dead lines) or should
          be re-enabled.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          <term>Orphaned <c>.bak</c> assets.</term> The <c>assets/</c> folder holds many
          <c>.pdf.bak</c> and <c>.svg.bak</c> files for the <q>How High The Moon</q>
          fragments. Remove them from version control if superseded.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          <term>Index and glossary.</term> The index is now enabled and populated (see
          above). A dedicated glossary or symbol list could still be added if desired.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          <term>Empty captions.</term> Some figures have empty
          <c>&lt;caption&gt;&lt;/caption&gt;</c> elements (for example the interval-grid
          rows). Populate or omit them.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          <term>House style.</term> A broader pass could standardise abbreviations
          (<q>etc;</q>/<q>eg;</q> &#8594; <q>etc.</q>/<q>e.g.</q>) and reduce the
          mid-sentence capitalisation of common nouns (Interval, Key, Chord, Root).
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

</chapter>
